# Onuros Community Software License 1.0

## Adoption notice

The Onuros project maintainer, identified on GitHub as Onuros-com, approved this
license for the project's original software. It applies to the original source,
tests, build files and project documentation distributed with this notice, to the
extent the relevant rights holder is authorized to grant these permissions.
Separately identified third-party material retains its own license. This notice
does not assign ownership or claim rights that a Licensor does not control.

The archived review draft is historical; this root LICENSE is the adopted text.

## 1. Covered material and parties

“Covered Material” means source code, executable code, or documentation that an
authorized rights holder expressly offers under this license. A “Licensor” is
such a rights holder, and “You” is anyone exercising the permissions below.
“Distribution” means providing a copy to another person or organization.

Each Licensor grants rights only in material and rights that the Licensor is
entitled to license. Separately identified third-party material is governed by
its own terms, as explained in section 7. This license does not transfer ownership
of the Covered Material or claim rights over material outside its scope.

## 2. Permission to use and build

Each Licensor gives You worldwide, nonexclusive copyright permission, without
license charges, to run and reproduce the Covered Material; study and change it;
combine it with other software; and distribute original or changed versions in
source or executable form. You may charge for copies, hosting, support, services,
or products that incorporate the Covered Material.

These permissions expressly include operating nodes and wallets, mining,
building applications, creating forks, and launching independent blockchains.
They do not depend on participation in the Onuros network, payment to an Onuros
fund, ownership of a token, or approval of an individual fork.

You may give recipients additional permissions in changes that You own and choose
terms for those changes. You may not withdraw or contradict the permissions this
license gives recipients in the original Covered Material. This license imposes
no obligation to publish Your private changes or supply source with an executable
distribution, subject to the separate obligations described in section 7.

## 3. Notices accompanying distribution

When You distribute Covered Material or a substantial portion of it, include a
copy of this license and retain the applicable copyright and attribution notices
that came with that material. Notices concerning removed material need not be
retained solely because that material appeared in an earlier version.

For source distributions, include the notices with the source. For executable
distributions, include them in accompanying documentation or another notice file
provided with the executable. An additional prominent advertisement or payment
is not required.

For changed distributions, provide a clear statement that changes were made and
identify the distributor responsible for that version. A complete change-by-change
history is not required. Do not describe a modified version as an unmodified
release supplied by an original Licensor.

Every recipient receives permission to the original Covered Material directly
from the relevant Licensors on these terms; recipients need no separate approval.

## 4. Identity and independent networks

This license supplies no trademark license for project names, logos, or service
marks. It does not limit truthful attribution, identification of compatibility,
or uses that applicable law permits without a trademark license.

Do not falsely claim that a Licensor endorses, maintains, audits, or guarantees
Your product or independent network. Permission to launch another blockchain
does not make that blockchain an official Onuros network. This section does not
restrict changes to consensus rules, economics, or application behavior in a fork.

## 5. Duration, compliance and restoration

Permissions continue for the duration of the applicable copyright and cannot be
withdrawn merely because a Licensor changes preferences, stops maintaining the
project, or publishes a later license version. They remain subject to compliance
with this version's conditions.

A material breach suspends the permissions needed for the noncompliant activity.
If You remedy that breach within thirty days after first receiving written notice
that reasonably identifies it, those permissions are restored automatically.
For a breach not remedied within that period, restoration requires the affected
Licensor's written permission. This provision does not erase responsibility for
conduct during a period of noncompliance.

A breach by one distributor does not remove the permissions of recipients who
remain compliant. Sections concerning notices, ownership, liability, and separate
third-party rights continue to apply where relevant after suspension.

## 6. No promise of performance; liability limits

The Covered Material is provided without a promise that it is correct, secure,
private, suitable for a particular purpose, free of infringement, or continuously
available. No Licensor is obliged by this license to provide support, maintenance,
updates, audits, or recovery services. Any separate written service commitment
must be assessed on its own terms.

To the extent applicable law allows, each Licensor disclaims warranties and
conditions concerning the Covered Material and is not liable for claims or losses
arising from its use, modification, distribution, or inability to operate. This
includes lost data, lost digital assets, lost revenue, and interruption of service,
regardless of the legal theory asserted or prior notice of the possibility.

Nothing here excludes liability or limits rights that applicable law does not
allow the parties to exclude or limit. Running tests or obtaining an audit does
not create a guarantee under this license.

## 7. Third-party material and other rights

This license does not replace licenses on third-party code, dependencies,
documents, or assets. Identify such material and preserve its required notices.
Where another license imposes source-disclosure, attribution, or other conditions,
comply with those conditions independently. This license does not assert that
any particular combination of software has compatible licensing terms.

The permission granted here concerns copyright. No express patent license is
included. The license gives no rights to someone else's private keys, accounts,
tokens, data, or trademarks. It neither grants an exemption from applicable law
nor restricts rights or exceptions that exist independently under that law.

## 8. Contributions, versions and interpretation

Submitting code, opening an issue, or controlling a repository does not by itself
transfer copyright or make a person a Licensor of someone else's material. A
contributor who expressly offers a contribution under this license grants these
permissions for the rights that contributor controls. Any assignment of ownership
requires a separate arrangement.

The version identified in the notice applying this license governs that material.
A later license version does not automatically replace it. Material may be offered
under additional terms only by a person authorized to grant the relevant rights.

If a provision cannot be enforced, the remaining provisions continue to apply to
the extent permitted by applicable law. No exclusive court, arbitration process,
or governing jurisdiction is selected by this text.

